              "id": "CVE-2026-29045",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Hono vulnerable to arbitrary file access via serveStatic vulnerability "
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Hono is a Web application framework that provides support for any JavaScript runtime. Prior to version 4.12.4, when using serveStatic together with route-based middleware protections (e.g. app.use(\u0026#39;/admin/*\u0026#39;, ...)), inconsistent URL decoding allowed protected static resources to be accessed without authorization. The router used decodeURI, while serveStatic used decodeURIComponent. This mismatch allowed paths containing encoded slashes (%2F) to bypass middleware protections while still resolving to the intended filesystem path. This issue has been patched in version 4.12.4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-29045",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-29045\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: hono\nFixed Version: 4.12.4\nLink: [CVE-2026-29045](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-29045)\nHono is a Web application framework that provides support for any JavaScript runtime. Prior to version 4.12.4, when using serveStatic together with route-based middleware protections (e.g. app.use('/admin/*', ...)), inconsistent URL decoding allowed protected static resources to be accessed without authorization. The router used decodeURI, while serveStatic used decodeURIComponent. This mismatch allowed paths containing encoded slashes (%2F) to bypass middleware protections while still resolving to the intended filesystem path. This issue has been patched in version 4.12.4.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-29045**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|hono|4.12.4|[CVE-2026-29045](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-29045)|\n\nHono is a Web application framework that provides support for any JavaScript runtime. Prior to version 4.12.4, when using serveStatic together with route-based middleware protections (e.g. app.use('/admin/*', ...)), inconsistent URL decoding allowed protected static resources to be accessed without authorization. The router used decodeURI, while serveStatic used decodeURIComponent. This mismatch allowed paths containing encoded slashes (%2F) to bypass middleware protections while still resolving to the intended filesystem path. This issue has been patched in version 4.12.4."
