            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-22036",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "undici: Undici: Denial of Service via excessive decompression steps"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Undici is an HTTP/1.1 client for Node.js. Prior to 7.18.0 and 6.23.0, the number of links in the decompression chain is unbounded and the default maxHeaderSize allows a malicious server to insert thousands compression steps leading to high CPU usage and excessive memory allocation. This vulnerability is fixed in 7.18.0 and 6.23.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-22036",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-22036\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: undici\nFixed Version: 7.18.2, 6.23.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-22036](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-22036)\nUndici is an HTTP/1.1 client for Node.js. Prior to 7.18.0 and 6.23.0, the number of links in the decompression chain is unbounded and the default maxHeaderSize allows a malicious server to insert thousands compression steps leading to high CPU usage and excessive memory allocation. This vulnerability is fixed in 7.18.0 and 6.23.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-22036**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|undici|7.18.2, 6.23.0|[CVE-2026-22036](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-22036)|\n\nUndici is an HTTP/1.1 client for Node.js. Prior to 7.18.0 and 6.23.0, the number of links in the decompression chain is unbounded and the default maxHeaderSize allows a malicious server to insert thousands compression steps leading to high CPU usage and excessive memory allocation. This vulnerability is fixed in 7.18.0 and 6.23.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.9",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.58.1"
        }
